{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>וכוין</b> — windows. So too in the Ishmaelite tongue." "<b>נגד ירושלם</b> — as it is written: \"and they pray toward their land\" (1 Kings 8:48)." "<b>וזימנין תלתא</b> — these are the three prayers that our early ones transmitted." "<b>בריך על ברכוהי</b> — like: \"and he blessed upon his knees\" (1 Kings 8:54)." "<b>ומצלא</b> — praying. So too in the Ishmaelite tongue."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The lemma is Aramaic; Ibn Ezra glosses it as Hebrew."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:20:11.788332826Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}